#### Limitations of these estimates.

Both findings rely on the per-question ℓHHq\ell\_{H}^{H\_{q}} proxy, which is a population-level signal rather than an individual worker’s signal. Replacing ℓHHq\ell\_{H}^{H\_{q}} with the confidence-based ℓH\ell\_{H} (Approach 1) does not give a directly comparable λ^\hat{\lambda} because the latter has only three values per worker. We report the cross-AI and cross-subject patterns as evidence that λ\lambda varies meaningfully and in interpretable directions, not as precise structural estimates.

